application   choupoSolve;
description   "NaCl crystalliser: saturation from the PITZER ion activity (Ksp = (gamma_pm*m_sat)^2). Feed is a SUPERSATURATED brine (post-evaporation, ~7.6 mol/kg); the unit drops it to saturation (6.144 mol/kg) and crystallises the excess.";
verbosity     3;

//  A brine case earns a stream table as much as any other -- and this one is
//  the corpus's witness that the table gets the SPECIES columns right where
//  the package resolves ions without an equilibrium network: n_Na / n_Cl
//  present, and NO pH column, because complete dissociation has no H+ network
//  to solve a pH from.  (The column used to be written as `0.000`, which does
//  not read as "absent" -- it reads as a strongly acidic brine.)
reports
{
    streamTable  {}
    massBalance  {}
}
